      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems the real issue here is that we aren\u0027t setting fSkPalette. I\u0027m fine with defaulting to palette 0 if out of range (essentially treating it like not specifying a palette index) but if it is out of range I\u0027m not sure the palette overrides should apply (since they\u0027re overrides for that palette index). On the other hand, it seems like specifying an out of range palette index and then specifying all the palette entry indexes as overrides (fully specifying a palette) should work.\n\nAnyhow this seems to be confusing css behavior https://www.w3.org/TR/css-fonts-4/#base-palette-desc . Need to make a note of that.",
